A||||1||msweldon||Another V6 bucking question.....||||1||
Z||000000||msweldon||10-11-2000||11:03 AM||||My 87gt 5spd has begun to buck, however not typically after its warmed up. e.g. ignition coil etc...  It only bucks for the first few minutes after I feather engage the clutch in and apply a constant neutral throttle(about 1/8 to 1/4) and let the engine torque itself through the rpm band.  Typical fuel saving driving while accelerating....  Then after a second or two of light neutral throttle the engine wants to fall back to idle almost as if I disengaged the clutch.  After another second or two the throttle seems to catch dumps the appropriate amount of fuel my gas pedal was originally depressed.  If I pump the gas pedal it will sometimes catch quicker but at the expense of the engine rocking violently.  My only remedy is to disengage the clutch when I notice the drop in rpm's and feather the clutch back in.  Most of the time this repeats again and again until the engine and clutch warms up.<P>Is it the IAC, MAP, TPS?  I run a true dual exhaust with no CAT or EGR.  the EGR tube and sensor have been plugged and has given me no troubles until now.<P>Hey Trav any ideas??<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>marc||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-11-2000||12:40 PM||||Check ECM for codes first, but my money is on the TPS.  Try testing its output (middle terminal) with an analog voltmeter.  Output voltage should vary smoothly with throttle position.<BR> <BR>Next guess would be the MAP sensor.<p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||1
